          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a deluge, then the Hindi for a whirlpool."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अकाल",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अकाल — akāl — \"a famine\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अकाल की वजह यह थी कि उस साल बारिश नहीं हुई। akāl kī vajah yah thī ki us sāl bāriś nahīṃ huī. The reason for the famine was that the rains failed that year."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अकाल (akāl) is Sanskrit akāla, \"a wrong or bad time\" (Monier-Williams). In Hindi it means a famine; the dictionary gives the older sense, and the step to a time of hunger is the language's own. A famine पड़ता है: it falls."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
